{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"childless-rhyolite-puma","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\n`docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md` calls the enforced module limit a soft cap and embeds dated tool inventory, machine state, measurements, findings, and capture debris as maintained procedure. The packaged `examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/SKILL.md` owns the audit phases. Ticket unafraid-homey-umbrette records the complexity ratchet, and scabby-slur-junk records a prior audit finding.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Rewrite the runbook as a rebar-project adapter to the packaged janitor workflow.\n- Retain project gate commands and the command inputs needed to run them.\n- Require rebar session logs and tickets for durable progress, decisions, and discovered work.\n- State that the module limit is an absolute CI gate sourced from `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n- Remove dated observations and capture debris from maintained procedure.\n- Refer to historical tickets when prior findings provide context.\n- Execute the documented read-only commands and run documentation link checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The runbook delegates audit phases to the packaged janitor skill.\n- [ ] Project-specific gate commands remain documented and executable.\n- [ ] Session logs and tickets are required as the durable artifacts for this repository.\n- [ ] The module limit is described as an absolute CI gate sourced from `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n- [ ] Dated machine state, measurements, findings, and capture debris are absent from maintained procedure.\n- [ ] Historical context points to tickets instead of restating incident narratives.\n- [ ] Documented read-only commands and documentation link checks pass.","id":"74dc-98da-4d2c-40b9","parent_id":"b8bf-a5aa-2f4d-44d4","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","accuracy","f38"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"F38 replace the maintenance audit snapshot with a project adapter"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787512792474002001,"uuid":"41954b79-1882-4164-9e3f-91f188b66cfa"}